<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Analyse research-unlocking items (the Biotech chips, and any modded equivalent) where
       they lie, instead of hauling them to a research bench.

       canStudyInPlace is vanilla's own flag, and Anomaly already ships three things that set
       it, so this switches on supported behaviour rather than adding any. Nothing is lost by
       skipping the bench: JobDriver_AnalyzeItem's duration is
       analysisDurationHours / pawn ResearchSpeed, with no term for the bench at all. See
       PLAN.md section 9.

       The not(canStudyInPlace) predicate skips comps that already carry the field, so a mod
       that sets it cannot end up with a duplicate node. success Always because a game
       without Biotech has no such comps to patch, and that is not a failure. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef/comps/li[@Class="CompProperties_CompAnalyzableUnlockResearch"][not(canStudyInPlace)]</xpath>
    <value>
      <canStudyInPlace>true</canStudyInPlace>
    </value>
    <success>Always</success>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
